=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A full four-phase sweep of the live lab found no fault matching the reported symptom. Phase A (infra_sweep + l2_snapshot) showed zero ACL rules, zero addressing anomalies, zero static ARP entries, correct default routes on both hosts, and no real MAC conflicts — the l2_snapshot's "duplicate" entries are the all-zeros MACs on universally-present kernel tunnel interfaces (tunl0, gre0, etc.), which are baseline on any Linux container. Phase B (ospf_snapshot + tc_snapshot) confirmed all six FRR routers healthy with vtysh responding, all OSPF neighbors in Full/DR or Full/Backup state, nine routes apiece, and every interface running the default pfifo_fast qdisc with no shaping or netem injection. Phase D (service_snapshot + pressure_sweep) showed all four web servers (web0.local–web3.local) answering HTTP 200 in ~3 ms from both client hosts, DNS resolving all names to the correct IPs via the single shared resolver at 10.200.0.2, localhost HTTP healthy on every web server process, and no CPU, socket, or stress-tool pressure anywhere in the topology.

The ticket's claim of "page dead all morning" is unconfirmed by the live state. There is no flap script, no tc rule, no ACL, no OSPF instability, and no dead daemon that could have caused or is currently causing the reported outage. The absence of any mechanism or historical trace means the claim cannot be substantiated from direct evidence.

Root cause: No reproducible fault — the network and all web services are fully operational at the time of diagnosis.

Fix: No corrective action required; advise the user to retest from their actual endpoint, as the issue does not reproduce in the lab.
=== END ===